2.7. Population and Mother Tongue
The question on mother tongue was collected from all persons in t he census households.
The information presented in table 2.7.1 shows that Khmer was the predominant mother tongue in
the country (95.8 percent) in 2019. Ethnic minority languages con stituted 2.9 percent. 1.3 percent
were people with a foreign language as mother tongue.
